          "start": 2.605,
          "end": 3.96,
          "en": "[Maximilian Schwarzmuller] So now that we know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.96,
          "end": 8.66,
          "en": "how we can build our site and what the implications are,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.66,
          "end": 9.86,
          "en": "let's take a look at",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.86,
          "end": 12.9,
          "en": "general deployment steps and considerations,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.9,
          "end": 16.17,
          "en": "no matter how you will build your site.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.17,
          "end": 18.38,
          "en": "The first step should always be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.38,
          "end": 20.7,
          "en": "that you double-check all your pages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.7,
          "end": 23.39,
          "en": "you make sure you added all the head metadata",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.39,
          "end": 26.36,
          "en": "to all your pages, titles, descriptions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.36,
          "end": 28.37,
          "en": "whatever else you might need.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.37,
          "end": 31.22,
          "en": "Of course, you wannna optimize your code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.22,
          "end": 34.06,
          "en": "remove console log statements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.06,
          "end": 37.52,
          "en": "shrink it as much as possible, things like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.52,
          "end": 40.33,
          "en": "And you wanna remove unnecessary dependencies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.33,
          "end": 44.54,
          "en": "and make your code as small and optimized as possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.54,
          "end": 46.99,
          "en": "So that is step number one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.99,
          "end": 51.26,
          "en": "Now once you did that, there is another kind of related step",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.26,
          "end": 54.25,
          "en": "which I still wanna list as a separate step.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.25,
          "end": 56.9,
          "en": "You wanna double-check your configuration,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.9,
          "end": 58.77,
          "en": "and you especially wanna consider",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.77,
          "end": 61.13,
          "en": "working with environment variables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.13,
          "end": 65.04,
          "en": "for data that might not be the same during development",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.04,
          "end": 66.73,
          "en": "and during production.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.73,
          "end": 69.1,
          "en": "For example, in our blog application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 69.1,
          "end": 72.61,
          "en": "we have an API route where I connect to a database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 72.61,
          "end": 76.13,
          "en": "and, at the moment, the way I connect here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.13,
          "end": 77.55,
          "en": "is always the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 77.55,
          "end": 81.39,
          "en": "My connection string is hard-coded in the API route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 81.39,
          "end": 83.64,
          "en": "so I always use the same user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 83.64,
          "end": 86.81,
          "en": "the same cluster, the same database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 86.81,
          "end": 89.957,
          "en": "It's more realistic that I want to use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 89.957,
          "end": 94.02000000000001,
          "en": "some development dummy database during development",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 94.02000000000001,
          "end": 96.2,
          "en": "and switch to a different database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 96.2,
          "end": 100.03,
          "en": "and maybe also an entirely different cluster and user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 100.03,
          "end": 101.59,
          "en": "for production.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 101.59,
          "end": 104.53,
          "en": "And, therefore, we want to swap",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 104.53,
          "end": 107.12,
          "en": "this connection string dynamically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 107.12,
          "end": 109.96000000000001,
          "en": "depending on the environment in which we're running.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 109.96000000000001,
          "end": 113.56,
          "en": "And that is something where environment variables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 113.56,
          "end": 115.57,
          "en": "will be able to help us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 115.57,
          "end": 118.24000000000001,
          "en": "Another use case could be API keys.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 118.24000000000001,
          "end": 122.06,
          "en": "If you're using the Google Maps SDK, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 122.06,
          "end": 124.51,
          "en": "These are things which you might wanna manage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 124.51,
          "end": 126.54,
          "en": "with environment variables.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 126.54,
          "end": 129.05,
          "en": "And therefore, that is, of course, also something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 129.05,
          "end": 131.943,
          "en": "we're going to explore in this course section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 133.16,
          "end": 136.8,
          "en": "Now once you did all of that, you should to do a test build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 136.8,
          "end": 141.8,
          "en": "and test your production-ready app on your local machine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 141.91,
          "end": 145.12,
          "en": "Since you just need a node server for running it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 145.12,
          "end": 148.23,
          "en": "and we already have Node.js installed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 148.23,
          "end": 150.31,
          "en": "building and running the application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 150.31,
          "end": 152.37,
          "en": "is rather straightforward.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 152.37,
          "end": 155.74,
          "en": "And we should do that to make sure that everything works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 155.74,
          "end": 157.95,
          "en": "that we're happy with the file sizes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 157.95,
          "end": 160.85,
          "en": "with the code bundle sizes, and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 160.85,
          "end": 163.25,
          "en": "Now that step, of course, can involve",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 163.25,
          "end": 165.3,
          "en": "that you go back to step one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 165.3,
          "end": 167.723,
          "en": "and implement further optimizations.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 168.61,
          "end": 170.36,
          "en": "Now once you're happy with all of that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 170.36,
          "end": 173.32,
          "en": "then it's time to finally deploy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 173.32,
          "end": 178.19,
          "en": "That is roughly how the deployment process will look like.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
